IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc30-forms-search`

-- ccc30-tests-forms-search.l4 -- tests for ccc30-forms-search.l4. Expected values are written by hand from the text of Forms 2, 4, 5.1 and 5.2
-- (raw lines 17469, 17487, 17913, 17923), never from the module's output. NOTHING means "not covered", never "no".

§ `Tests -- Form 2 and Form 4, the Note on the date of birth`

-- "The date of birth of the accused may be mentioned on the information or indictment."
#ASSERT `form 2 note the date of birth of the accused may be mentioned` `an information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 2 note the date of birth of the accused may be mentioned` `an indictment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Any other document is outside the words of the Note: not covered (not "may not").
#ASSERT `form 2 note the date of birth of the accused may be mentioned` `a summons` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 2 note the date of birth of the accused may be mentioned` `a warrant for arrest` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 4 note the date of birth of the accused may be mentioned` `an information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 4 note the date of birth of the accused may be mentioned` `an indictment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 4 note the date of birth of the accused may be mentioned` `an undertaking` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- Form 5.1, Notice of execution of a search warrant`

-- First sentence: "If anything is seized ... the things that were seized may be brought before the court at (address)."
#ASSERT `form 5.1 the things that were seized may be brought before the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Nothing seized: the "If" is unmet, and the text is silent about the things (a "may" limited by its "If").
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `form 5.1 the things that were seized may be brought before the court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `form 5.1 the things that were seized may be brought before the court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Second sentence: "if the peace officer ... filed with that court a report ..., you may obtain a copy of the report from the clerk of that court."
#ASSERT `form 5.1 the person may obtain a copy of the report from the clerk of that court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `form 5.1 the person may obtain a copy of the report from the clerk of that court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the name is a "may" that gives a power or liberty and its "If" gate is unmet; the text limits the grant in its own wording and is silent outside the limit, so the answer is NOTHING, not a "may not" (name-test sweep, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
#ASSERT `form 5.1 the person may obtain a copy of the report from the clerk of that court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- Form 5.2, Report to a justice`

-- Returned to the person lawfully entitled: the receipt shall be attached.
#ASSERT `form 5.2 the receipt for the thing seized shall be attached to the report` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not returned (it is being detained): "in which case" is a condition that is unmet, so the receipt limb does not apply.
#ASSERT `form 5.2 the receipt for the thing seized shall be attached to the report` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Being detained: the location and manner shall be indicated; not detained: that limb does not apply.
#ASSERT `form 5.2 the location and manner of the detention shall be indicated in the report` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.2 the location and manner of the detention shall be indicated in the report` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "or, if applicable, the person by whom it is being detained": detained AND a person is detaining it.
#ASSERT `form 5.2 the person by whom the thing seized is being detained shall be indicated in the report` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.2 the person by whom the thing seized is being detained shall be indicated in the report` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.2 the person by whom the thing seized is being detained shall be indicated in the report` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.2 the person by whom the thing seized is being detained shall be indicated in the report` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
